        "title": "Tips to visit Pashupatinath Temple",
        "text": "Pashupatinath Temple is spread over a huge area. One has to walk from the gate. If you explore only the main temple.you will.walk around 2km. There's a free service to put your shoes in a bag & leave at a counter. The service is smooth & efficient. \n\nOur first visit was on a Saturday afternoon which was too crowded to get a darshan. We went again early in the morning around 6.30am & it was easy to get a darshan. There was a queue to do pooja but we didn't want to stand & wait. Theres a shorter queue to  just do pranams in front of the main idol. That  is very easily accessible & moves quickly.So here are the tips:\n1. Visit early in the day, queues are shorter \n2. Use the free shoe storage service . It's very efficient.\n3. Afternoons get crowded & hot. So it's difficult to walk on the paved stones bare feet.\n4. You can walk to the Guhayeswari Temple which is a shaktipeeths from inside. We did that & didn't mind the walk.",
