        "title": "Beware Forced Tours, Amazing Aarati Ceremony",
        "text": "We visited Pashupatinath Temple one evening to attend the Aarati ceremony. Upon entry, and man told us he would show us where the ceremony was and then began taking us on a full tour. I should have just walked away, but my kindness got the best of me and I allowed him to show us a few things before I insisted that I wanted to grab a good seat for the ceremony. At that point, he pressed us into paying him an absurd amount for his \"tour\".  We did not pay the price he wanted, but instead gave him 200 rupees. Again, as a person who has traveled all over Asia, I should have known better, but beware. If you don't want a tour, be firm with these \"guides\". The Aarati ceremony was amazing though, really powerful watching the ceremony with cremations occurring in the background. I always feel a little strange attending religious ceremonies for religions that I do not belong to, but we felt very welcomed by others around us. Highly recommend while you are in Kathmandu.",
