      {
        "review_id": 1051352992,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r1051352992-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Har Har Mahadev 🔱🔱",
        "text": "This temple is not a Jyotirlinga, yet it is one of the most sacred and important religious place for Hindus. The temple is deeply connected with Lord Shiva and has many fascinating stories and legends associated with it, which make the visit even more meaningful.\n          The Temple complex is very huge and beautifully spread out, with many small temples dedicated to different deities are inside the premises. Built in Traditional Nepalese Pagoda Style architecture, features a square, two-tiered roof covered in gold plating, intricate carved wooden structure and four silver plated main doors.\n           As a walk around, you can feel the spiritual atmosphere everywhere. The Shiva Linga here is ‘Chaturmukh’, which mean it has Four Faces representing different aspects of Lord Shiva. All four side doors for Darshan opens at 9:30 am, before that, devotees can have Darshan from the front side. The entire Darshan process is simple and well organised. There is no unnecessary pressure from pandits asking for money for rituals, thus we were able to complete our darshan comfortably and peacefully.\n             The Temple is located on the banks of the Holy Bagmati River. In the evening, a beautiful and peaceful Aarti is performed by the river, which is truly divine to witness. On the opposite side of the river is the Samshan Ghat, reminding us of the cycle of life and death, which is an important belief in Hinduism.\n               Mobile phones are allowed inside the temple complex, but photography is strictly not permitted. When we visited, we saw many “Naga Sadhus” probably because we went a day after Shivratri. Their presence added to the spiritual aura of the place.\n              Prasad can be purchased from the stalls outside the temple complex. You will also find Rudraksha mala being sold here. Overall this temple has a very strong and positive vibration that can truly be felt from within. It is a place that gives peace to the mind and soul.\n              May Lord Shiva bless everyone who visits this Holy Temple.",
