        "title": "Pashupatinath Aarti",
        "text": "We went to Pashupatinath mainly for the evening Aarti at 6.30 pm. Entering the gate of the complex felt like stepping straight from Nepal into India. Aarti is carried out on the ghats. The priests performing the Aarti were consummate professionals and indeed the crowd was enraptured for the almost 1 hour duration. Be aware that there are cremations taking place right at the ghats so can be quite emotional. A boon to have a place such as this within Kathmandu as in India often need to travel a fair bit to reach such a location.",
